  data: {
    LLM: "Starting Hand Selection: Only play if your first two cards are both 8 or lower with no pair. If your hole card is paired with your upcard, or if you show a high card like a King or Queen, strongly consider folding.\n\nBoard Reading: Pay close attention to your opponents' upcards. If you hold A-3 in the hole but three other Aces are showing, your hand is much weaker. Conversely, if many low cards are showing, your medium-low hand gains value.\n\nPosition Play: In later betting rounds, acting first with a strong low hand can be disadvantageous (you can't gain information). However, with a marginal hand in late position, you can make better decisions based on opponents' actions. The bring-in position (highest card showing) is at a significant disadvantage.",
